DELETE FROM public.junior_listening_exercises WHERE volume='elective4' AND unit='U3';
Tom: I''m thinking about the whale watching camp. We''d help a real research team.
Lucy: That sounds exciting. What would you actually do there?
Tom: We''d follow whales in a boat and take photos of their fins to tell them apart.
Lucy: I''d rather try the diving camp, where you learn to use underwater cameras.
Tom: Why diving? Isn''t it a bit dangerous for beginners?
Lucy: Maybe, but I really want to see coral reefs with my own eyes.
Tom: Fair enough. Let''s each choose our own camp and share our stories afterwards.', 'Lucy 问 Tom 选了哪个海洋夏令营;Tom 想去观鲸营,能协助真正的研究团队,跟踪鲸并拍鳍照辨认;Lucy 更想去潜水营学用水下摄像机,因为想亲眼看珊瑚礁;两人决定各选各的,之后分享见闻。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which camp is Tom thinking of joining?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The whale watching camp.","The diving camp.","The sailing camp.","The fishing camp."]},{"q":"What would Tom do at his camp?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Clean the beaches all day.","Follow whales and photograph their fins.","Drive a research ship.","Catch fish for dinner."]},{"q":"Why does Lucy prefer the diving camp?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She wants to see coral reefs herself.","It is much cheaper.","It is closer to home.","Her teacher chose it for her."]},{"q":"What is Tom''s worry about diving?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It takes too long.","It may be dangerous for beginners.","There are no cameras.","It is boring for beginners."]},{"q":"What do they finally decide to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Join the same camp together.","Stay at home all summer.","Each choose a camp and share stories later.","Give up both camps."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3');
Scientists divide the main types of whales by the way they feed.
Whales use sounds both to talk to one another and to find their way.
Each whale has slightly different fins, which help researchers tell them apart.
By studying whales, we learn a great deal about the health of the ocean.', '鲸是海里最大、最聪明的生物之一;科学家按进食方式划分鲸的主要类型;鲸用声音彼此交流并辨别方向;每头鲸的鳍略有不同,帮助研究者辨认;通过研究鲸,我们能了解海洋的健康状况。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How are the main types of whales divided?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By their colour.","By their age.","By where they sleep.","By the way they feed."]},{"q":"What do whales use sounds for?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To communicate and to find their way.","Only to scare ships away.","Only to sleep better.","To break the ice."]},{"q":"What helps researchers tell whales apart?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Their names.","Their slightly different fins.","Their numbers painted on them.","Their songs alone."]},{"q":"What does the passage say about whales'' intelligence?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are among the most foolish animals.","They cannot learn anything.","They are among the most intelligent sea creatures.","They are no smarter than fish."]},{"q":"Why is studying whales useful?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It helps us catch more of them.","It makes the sea smaller.","It has no real purpose.","It teaches us about the health of the ocean."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3');
Student: It''s huge! People call it a moving laboratory on the sea, don''t they?
Guide: That''s right. We can study samples within hours of bringing them up.
Student: How deep can your robots go?
Guide: Our vehicle Faxian can dive far below the surface to survey the sea floor.
Student: And it brings samples back to the ship?
Guide: Yes, tons of geological samples that our scientists then examine here.
Student: No wonder Kexue is in a league of its own. Thank you for the tour!', '讲解员欢迎学生登上“科学号”科考船;学生说它被称作海上移动实验室;讲解员说采样后几小时内就能研究;深潜器“发现号”能下潜到海底进行勘测并带回大量地质样本供船上科学家研究;学生感叹科学号独领风骚并致谢。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Kexue often called?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A moving laboratory on the sea.","A floating hotel.","A fishing boat.","A war ship."]},{"q":"How soon can the team study the samples?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["After several years.","Within hours of bringing them up.","Never on the ship.","Only back on land."]},{"q":"What does the vehicle Faxian do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It flies above the ship.","It cleans the deck.","It dives deep to survey the sea floor.","It carries the students home."]},{"q":"What does Faxian bring back?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Fresh fish for lunch.","Photos of the sky.","Empty boxes.","Tons of geological samples."]},{"q":"How does the student feel about Kexue at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is unusual and impressive.","It is too small to matter.","It is just an ordinary boat.","It is not worth visiting."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3');
Tiny pieces of plastic harm fish, birds and other marine creatures.
Shockingly, plastic has even been found in the tap water we drink.
Some experts say we should tax plastic bottles so that people use fewer.
Every small action, from using less plastic to cleaning a beach, can help.', '塑料污染已成为海洋最大的危险之一;细小的塑料碎片伤害鱼、鸟和其他海洋生物;令人震惊的是,塑料甚至已在我们喝的自来水中被发现;一些专家说应对塑料瓶征税,以便人们少用;从少用塑料到清理海滩,每个小行动都有帮助。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is described as one of the biggest dangers to the oceans?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Loud noise.","Plastic pollution.","Cold weather.","Too many ships."]},{"q":"Where has plastic shockingly been found?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["In the sun.","In the moon.","In our tap water.","In the desert sand."]},{"q":"What do some experts suggest doing?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Drinking less water.","Catching more fish.","Banning all beaches.","Taxing plastic bottles."]},{"q":"What harms fish, birds and other creatures?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Tiny pieces of plastic.","Fresh rain.","Soft music.","Warm sunshine."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about small actions?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Small actions are useless.","Each small action can help.","Only governments can help.","Nothing can be done."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3');
Diver: That''s deep. Will we use the manned submersible?
Captain: Yes, but only two of us can go inside the small capsule.
Diver: What''s our main task down there?
Captain: We''ll film the coral and collect a few samples from the sea floor.
Diver: Should I worry about the cold and the pressure?
Captain: The capsule keeps us safe, but follow every step of the plan exactly.
Diver: Understood. I''ll check all the cameras and lights tonight.', '船长说明天下潜约三百米深;潜水员问是否用载人潜水器;船长说会用,但小舱只能进两人;主要任务是拍珊瑚并从海底采几份样本;潜水员问要不要担心寒冷和压力;船长说舱内安全,但要严格按计划每一步执行;潜水员表示今晚检查所有摄像机和灯。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How deep will tomorrow''s dive go?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["About three metres.","About thirty kilometres.","About three hundred metres.","Just below the surface."]},{"q":"How many people can go inside the capsule?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The whole crew.","Exactly ten.","Nobody at all.","Only two."]},{"q":"What is the main task during the dive?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To film coral and collect samples.","To catch large fish.","To race another submersible.","To clean the ship''s deck."]},{"q":"What does the captain tell the diver to do about safety?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Ignore the plan and improvise.","Follow every step of the plan exactly.","Stay on the ship instead.","Swim outside the capsule."]},{"q":"What will the diver do tonight?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Go straight to sleep.","Cancel the whole dive.","Check all the cameras and lights.","Repaint the submersible."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3');
Yet the sea covers most of our planet and shapes our climate.
Exploring it may lead to new medicines, food and sources of energy.
It can also help scientists predict events such as earthquakes.
The more we understand the sea, the better we can protect it.', '人类对世界海洋的探索还不到百分之五;然而海洋覆盖了地球大部分并影响着气候;探索海洋也许会带来新药、新食物和新能源;还能帮助科学家预测地震等事件;我们越了解海洋,就越能保护它。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How much of the oceans have people explored?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Almost all of it.","Exactly half of it.","None of it at all.","Less than five percent."]},{"q":"What does the sea do to our planet?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It covers most of it and shapes the climate.","It makes the land disappear.","It has no effect on us.","It stops the weather completely."]},{"q":"What might exploring the sea lead to?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Less food for everyone.","New medicines, food and energy.","The end of all medicine.","Fewer scientists."]},{"q":"What event can sea research help predict?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Birthday parties.","Football matches.","Earthquakes.","School exams."]},{"q":"What is the main message of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["We should never study the sea.","The sea is not important.","Exploration is a waste of time.","Understanding the sea helps us protect it."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE volume='elective4' AND unit='U3';

Last week, a Chinese research team announced that its manned submersible, named after a dragon, had successfully reached a depth of about seven kilometres in the Pacific Ocean. Three scientists spent hours in the small capsule, using powerful lights and cameras to study the dark sea floor that human eyes had never seen.

During the dive, the team logged several new sea creatures and collected rare minerals, achievements that greatly extend our knowledge of marine life. "Every voyage adds another page to our book of knowledge about the sea," one scientist said.

Why does such work matter? Because the ocean covers most of our planet, exploring it may bring new medicines and help us protect a fragile world for future generations.', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["A Chinese research team announced that its manned submersible had successfully reached a depth of about seven kilometres.","Using powerful lights and cameras, the scientists studied the dark sea floor that human eyes had never seen.","During the dive, the team logged several new sea creatures and collected rare minerals.","Because the ocean covers most of our planet, exploring it may bring new medicines and help us protect a fragile world."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"The submersible reached at a depth of seven kilometres.","correct":"The submersible reached a depth of seven kilometres.","note":"reach 是及物动词,后面直接跟宾语,不加 at。"},{"wrong":"The team logged new creatures which extend our knowledge.","correct":"The team logged new creatures, which extended our knowledge.","note":"非限制性定语从句前加逗号;且与主句时态一致用过去式 extended。"},{"wrong":"Named after a dragon, the team built the submersible.","correct":"Named after a dragon, the submersible carried the team into the deep.","note":"过去分词作状语的逻辑主语须与主句主语一致(被命名的是潜水器,不是团队)。"}]'::jsonb, '【海洋探索新闻报道结构】
标题:A Breakthrough Beneath the Waves
第1段 导语:A research team announced that … had successfully reached … (时间/地点/谁/做了什么)
第2段 细节+意义:During the dive, the team logged … and collected …, which extended … 加一句引语 "…," one scientist said.
第3段 为何探海:Because the ocean covers most of our planet, exploring it may … and help us protect …', 2, 'elective4', 'U3');

